<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joan of England, Queen of Sicily</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1165">1165</a>–1199</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> was a daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-aquitaine">Eleanor of Aquitaine</a>. She married King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-ii-of-sicily">William II of Sicily</a> in 1177 and, after his death, was freed by her brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/richard-i-of-england">Richard I</a>, whom she accompanied on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/third-crusade">Third Crusade</a>. In 1196 she married Raymond VI of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>, bringing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agenais">Agenais</a> as her dowry, and was mother of Raymond VII. She died in childbirth in 1199.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joan-of-england-queen-of-sicily.jpg" alt="Joan of England, Queen of Sicily" width="254" height="392" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joan_of_England.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Dynastic marriages tied the house to the great royal families: Raymond V married Constance, sister of Louis VII of France, and Raymond VI married <b>Joan of England</b>, sister of Richard I, who brought the Agenais as her dowry.</blockquote><a href="/empire/county-of-toulouse">County of Toulouse · Governance &amp; Law</a></li></ul></section>
